And it was all going so well ...

This was the best game I have ever played without cheating. I have recently
hit on a combination of techniques that help me extend my lifespan in the
early game. First, obvious stuff that has all been gone over many times in
the group: don't take risks on unidentified stuff, sinks, fountains, etc.,
take my time, stuff like that. Next, playing a Valk, I stay on DL1 until
XL7; if I get hungry, I wait until fainting and then pray - almost always
works for as much as I use it. I fight exclusively with my dagger(s) and
pick up any daggers I see, until I am Expert in dagger; thereafter I throw
daggers as ranged weapons.  Like I said, obvious stuff.  Unfortunately I
usually lose my pet doing this.

Anyway, this Valk was lucky. Nice armor showed up pretty soon, and I was in
negative AC before DL5. Two altars on DL4 got me Mojo. Found a couple of
shops, resisted temptation to steal (without a pet, quite dangerous). Got
down to Sokoban, did Sokoban easily (bag of holding, yaay), back up and run
the Mines for the luckstone (no touchstone this time though). 2 of my own
bones levels and 1 from hearse helped improve me too.

Then, WOW. A hearse bones level around DL13 provided MONDO loot. This must
have been an experienced player's stash: there was a bag of holding with
dozens of scrolls and wands, an ice chest with chamaeleon corpses, and
(uh-oh!) a hostile Archon wielding Sunsword. Yikes! Again I got lucky:
after zapping him with a wand of teleport a few times, he got stuck in a
diagonal tunnel that was probably a dwarf's pickaxe trail.  So I could loot
at leisure.

Unfortunately I didn't know that looting a cursed bag of holding causes
stuff to disappear. I decided (as usual) to be spoiled, and found out that
a wand of cancellation removes the curse without bothering anything inside,
so although I lost all the potions (8, probably all holy water) I was able
to save lots of scrolls, wands, and gold. And gauntlets of power, the Eye
of Aethopica, and a wand of wishing?? WOW!

Now I'm feeling pretty powerful. I wish for GDSM, speed boots, a shield of
reflection, a fireproof robe (I've got lots of spellbooks by now). The Orb
of Fate for level teleportation. Wear the Eye for ESP and warning.  I wish
for the Mitre of Holiness ... ugh, it's lawful and I'm not. I'll leave it
in the stash. Last wish therefore was for a helm of brilliance. I make some
holy water, get my stuff blessed, do the quest. Leave one BOH in the stash
back at DL4, take the other along.

I go back down, collecting everything in the BOH. Somehow I get to the
castle without seeing Medusa. I make a mistake and throw Mojo at an eel -
oops, it is underwater! Freeze the water, dig, there it is, whew. Finish
the castle, another /oW; I'll save it for later.

Continuing down, using the Orb to return to the stash periodically to
unload, Valley of the Dead. I decide to donate for protection, my first
time doing this, I get 3 points. My AC is now around -25. I continue into
Gehennom, eventually I find and defeat Vlad's Tower. ok, got Bell and
Candelabrum, where's the book? I can't find the Wizard's Tower yet, must
not be deep enough.

I decide to try twoweaponing Mojo and a silver sabre and it is a scream.
Take that, ye demons! Unfortunately, not wielding my shield, I am no longer
reflecting. Most dragon blasts and wands miss me, but ... in Orcustown, a
black dragon gets through and destroys my GDSM and my robe! AAAAAAUGH!!!

(I am not remembering something right, because at this point I do not have
any wishes left.) But I make SDSM out of some scales I picked up, and I
have another robe that I make fireproof. And here's where I get greedy. I
want the Mitre on my head. Being Neutral I haven't been able to pick it up
yet. Earlier I tried a helm of opposite alignment, but it made me Chaotic,
not Lawful. But I look it up in the spoilers and I realize now it's random
every time. I've got a few dozen holy water, so let's try again ... I
manage to pick up the Mitre, yay. I take off the helm, but now I still
can't put ON the Mitre.... I will have to convert to Lawful to do this.

Fortunately I remember that the Minetown altar is Lawful, so I go there.
But I am "piously aligned". So I have to get sinful, fast.... I murder all
the guards and shopkeepers, no luck. I offer a human corpse on the altar -
stupid! now it's a chaotic altar, I needed lawful! And I'm still pious, oh
well, let's keep going ... Uh-oh, Yeenonough is summoning lots of stuff
.... DYWYPI?


